### Food Delivery Platform - Delivery Partner Service
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (named requests pass ids between calls).
###
### delivery-partner-service owns the partners: registration (from UserRegistered, or on the partner's first call),
### profile (vehicle and city) and the account status (an admin suspends or reactivates, audited).
### delivery-service keeps what partners are doing: going online (PUT /me/availability), the assignment of
### deliveries, /availability, /stats and a partner's deliveries. The API Gateway sends each path to its service, so
### the web application uses the same URLs as before.
###
### Caller identity: the access token of a sign-in below (Authorization: Bearer); its role must be
###   DELIVERY_PARTNER for /delivery/partners/me, PLATFORM_ADMIN for /admin/**

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
# The services' shared secret of the internal APIs: the dev profile's value (INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN elsewhere)
@internalServiceToken = dev-internal-service-token
@service = http://localhost:8099

@partnerEmail = sunil.rider@example.com
@partnerPassword = Rider1234
@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123

@partnerId = {{partnerLogin.response.body.$.userId}}
# Every call carries the access token of a sign-in above (valid 15 minutes: sign in again after that).
@partnerToken = {{partnerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}


### ============================ SETUP ============================

### 1. Register a delivery partner (409 if it already exists: fine). UserRegistered creates the partner here.
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{partnerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{partnerPassword}}",
  "fullName": "Sunil Rao",
  "phone": "+919900445566",
  "role": "DELIVERY_PARTNER"
}

### 2. Logins -> partnerId, adminToken
# @name partnerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{partnerEmail}}", "password": "{{partnerPassword}}" }

###
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }


### ============================ PARTNER ============================

### 3. My profile (OFFLINE, readyToWork false until vehicle and city are set)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/partners/me
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}

### 4. Vehicle and city: published as DeliveryPartnerChanged (PROFILE_UPDATED), delivery-service keeps a copy
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/partners/me
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vehicleType": "SCOOTER", "vehicleNumber": "ka05xy9999", "city": "Bengaluru" }

### 5. Go online: delivery-service's API (it decides availability together with the deliveries)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/partners/me/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "AVAILABLE" }

### 6. My profile again: status AVAILABLE, as delivery-service reported it (DeliveryPartnerStatusChanged)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/partners/me
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}

### 7. Validation: an unknown vehicle type and a blank number -> 400 with the fields
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/partners/me
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vehicleType": "HOVERBOARD", "vehicleNumber": "", "city": "Bengaluru" }


### ============================ ADMIN ============================

### 8. Partners in a city, by status (OFFLINE, AVAILABLE, BUSY, SUSPENDED); q = part of the name or phone
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners?city=Bengaluru&status=AVAILABLE&q=sunil
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 9. One partner
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 10. Deactivate (suspend): 409 while the partner is on a delivery (reassign it first). delivery-service stops
###     offering them deliveries (an offer not accepted yet goes back to the queue).
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Vehicle documents expired" }

### 11. The partner cannot go online now: 409 (delivery-service)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/partners/me/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "AVAILABLE" }

### 12. Activate again (the partner starts OFFLINE and goes online themselves)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "New documents checked" }

### 13. The partner's audit trail (newest first; also in admin-service's platform-wide audit log)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 14. Not this service: partners per status right now, and the partner's deliveries (delivery-service)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}/deliveries
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ======================= INTERNAL (not through the gateway) =======================

### 15. Once, on an installation from before this service existed: take over the partners delivery-service kept
###     (profile, suspension, current status). Partners already here are left as they are, so repeating is safe.
POST {{service}}/api/v1/internal/delivery-partners/import
X-Service-Token: {{internalServiceToken}}

### 16. What delivery-service asks when a partner's DeliveryPartnerChanged event has not reached it yet
GET {{service}}/api/v1/internal/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}
X-Service-Token: {{internalServiceToken}}

### 17. Send every audit record again to admin-service's platform-wide audit log (safe to repeat)
POST {{service}}/api/v1/internal/audit-logs/events/republish
X-Service-Token: {{internalServiceToken}}

### 18. Through the gateway the internal API does not exist: 404
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/internal/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}


### ======================= EVENTS (Kafka) =======================
### Publishes DeliveryPartnerChanged (REGISTERED, PROFILE_UPDATED, SUSPENDED, ACTIVATED; key = partnerUserId) and
### AdminActionAudited through its transactional outbox.
### Consumes UserRegistered (new partners) and DeliveryPartnerStatusChanged (what delivery-service reports).
### Messages: Kafka UI http://localhost:8090

GET http://localhost:8091/subjects/fooddelivery.delivery-partner.changed-value/versions/latest

### Health and Swagger UI (http://localhost:8099/swagger-ui.html)
GET {{service}}/actuator/health
